@startuml sequence-portal-features
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: how the portal decides which features to show, and how an administrator switches one at runtime
'       through the catalog's instance settings (portal.features) instead of a rebuild.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram. Scope: the portal (feature store + Administration › Features) against the
'       catalog's settings API; the public read is a proposal.
' Source: EvilFlowersCatalog develop apps/core/settings_store.py, apps/api/views/instance_settings.py,
'         apps/core/capabilities.py (#212 as implemented, 2026-11-17); elvira-portal src/features/ (2026-11-17)
' =============================================================================

title Portal features: build default, catalog setting, catalog capability (proposal, 2026-11-17)

actor Reader as reader
actor Administrator as admin
participant "Portal\nfeature store" as store <<proposed>> <<focus>>
participant "Administration ›\nFeatures" as page <<proposed>>
participant "Catalog API\n/api/v1/settings" as api

== Every page load ==
reader -> store : open portal
store -> store : localStorage (last answer)\nelse build default (ELVIRA_FEATURES)
store -[$accent_msg()]> api : <b>GET settings?public=true&include=capabilities</b> (no token)
api --> store : {response: [{key: portal.features, value}], capabilities}
store -> store : enabled = capability ≠ off\n∧ (setting ?? build default)
store --> reader : menu, routes, tabs for enabled features only

== An administrator switches a feature ==
admin -> page : Assistant: Off
page -> api : PUT settings/portal.features {value: {assistant: false}}\n(superuser)
api --> page : 200 {value, source: stored}
page -> store : update snapshot (admin sees it now)
note right of api : Next reader request reads the\nnew row (Redis cache invalidated\non commit, settings_store).

$legend_live_proposed()

caption The first layer that says "off" wins: a capability the catalog reports off, then the stored setting, then the build default.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · elvira-portal · docs/diagrams/sequence-portal-features.puml
@enduml
